# THE CAVES ARE ROOFED (GenAbove, docs/ABOVE.md S3): a hall stands under a lid of
# rock, terraced in plateaus, open only over the shafts and the tears the day
# comes down through. Under a roof from above the plateau over the player is
# cut at the section plane (43_above), its outline chalked; over the shoulder the
# roof is a ceiling overhead, and a tear's column of daylight falls through it.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/cave-roofs.tour --seed=7 --realm=underground --hour=12
coast calm
wait 1.0
near under_roof
wait 1.0
await above_cut 4
shot 01-under-the-roof-from-above-cut
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
await above_whole 3
wait 1.0
shot 02-under-the-roof-over-the-shoulder with shoulder
mouse 0,-300 0.5
wait 1.0
shot 03-up-at-the-roof with shoulder
near shaft_pool
wait 1.5
shot 04-daylight-through-a-tear with shoulder
